  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "10.0.2: Saving a picture now works on Blazor Server. Two faults stood in the way. The drawn picture was handed to Blazor as a Blob, which answered \"Supplied value is not a typed array or blob\"; it is handed over as a typed array instead. And the component used ConfigureAwait(false) throughout, so raising OnError rendered the host off the dispatcher and ended the circuit — it now stays on the renderer's synchronization context.\n\n10.0.1: Size the editor without its scoped stylesheet. A host that does not link its scoped-CSS bundle — which is every host with no scoped CSS of its own — got a canvas with no height, showing a strip of picture at the top of an empty box. The layout the component cannot do without is now written on the elements themselves, and the stylesheet holds only what is cosmetic.\n\n10.0.0: First release. Crop, rotate, flip, scale and reset an image, with a toolbar or driven entirely from code through @ref. The edited picture comes back as a stream rather than a string, so it is not bounded by the SignalR message size on Blazor Server.",
